.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
A minimal user‑mode spin lock based on an atomic integer\&. The lock stores the managed thread ID of the owning thread\&. A value of \fR0\fP means the lock is free\&. 

This lock is designed for very short critical sections where kernel-level synchronization would be too expensive\&. It uses Interlocked\&.Exchange(ref int, int) to acquire the lock and Thread\&.SpinWait(int) for contention handling\&.

.PP
The lock is non‑reentrant, non‑fair, and does not block the thread\&. Instead, it spins until the lock becomes available or until a timeout expires\&. This makes it suitable for high‑performance user‑mode synchronization primitives such as barriers\&.

.PP
Ownership is determined by comparing the stored thread ID with Thread\&.CurrentThread\&.ManagedThreadId\&. Only the owning thread is allowed to release the lock\&. 
